jobDescription:
Who we are

Neotalent Conclusion is one of the leading Iberian specialists providing services in Information Technology and Engineering services. As part of the Netherlands-based organization Conclusion, which has an ecosystem of over 25 companies and 3,600 employees, we are focused on increasing the technological capacity of our clients and the digital transformation of their application ecosystems.

We are talent specialists, attracting the best people and combining them with the needs of the most ambitious projects, at the right time. Our success comes from our investments in innovation, our focus on results, and, above all, the guarantee that our people will have happy and rewarding careers.

With over 25 years of solid experience, Neotalent Conclusion has established its presence in key locations, including Lisbon, Porto, and Madrid. The company currently has more than 950 professionals in the different areas in which it operates.




Neotalent, the responsive people.




Find out more about us at https://www.neotalentconclusion.com.




Role Overview

We are looking for a Junior .NET Developer to join our teams in a challenging international technology environment focused on building and enhancing innovative software solutions used by millions of users worldwide.




You will participate in the full software development lifecycle, from requirements analysis and solution design to implementation, testing, maintenance, and continuous improvement of business-critical applications.




What you will do

Analyse business and functional requirements and contribute to the definition of technical specifications;
Design, develop, and maintain scalable software solutions using Microsoft .NET technologies, with a focus on C#;
Perform feasibility studies and propose technical solutions aligned with business needs and product objectives;
Design, model, and implement database solutions, ensuring performance, reliability, and maintainability;
Execute unit, integration, and performance testing, support debugging activities, and contribute to the continuous improvement of application quality and documentation.




What you are like

Between 1 - 3 years of experience in software development area;
Experience with Microsoft .NET technologies, particularly C# development;
Knowledgeable in relational and/or NoSQL database modelling, design, and implementation;
Familiar with software testing practices, debugging techniques, and quality assurance processes;
Comfortable working within Agile environments and using version control systems such as Git.




Why join us

Work on challenging projects for big clients;
Learn more about emerging technologies;
Possibility of working remotely;
Design your career plan;
Access to continuous training and certifications;
Evolve through our internal mobility program;
... and much more!
